-- program-of-at u m c fuel: (refused , definitions). definitions: the entry and every definition
-- reachable from it that quotes, each (g , code), its code given by u; refused: those that do not,
-- each (g , verdict). Whether a definition is in the fragment is decided after the encoder's passes
-- have removed what no result depends on (lib/x86.cub): a proof argument's code may use composition
-- and never be computed. The walk runs while there is a definition to do, at most fuel steps
prog-run-at : (Word → Opt Code) → Word → Prog → Lst (Word × Verdict) × Lst (Word × Code)
prog-run-at u fuel st =
  (let r = %welimP (λ _ → Prog → Prog) fuel (λ s → s)
             (λ j go s → case fst s return (λ _ → Prog) of
                lnil → s
                lcons g rest → go (prog-step-at u s)) st
   in (snd (snd (snd r)) , fst (snd (snd r))))
